From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:17:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0883/3799] soh: rename D_8016A578 -> gUnusedTotalTime

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: volatile OSTime sitting inside the RSP/RDP total-time block between gRSPOtherTotalTime and gRDPTotalTime, but never read or written; the slot's original meaning is unknown.
Defined in soh/src/code/speed_meter.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/speed_meter.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/speed_meter.c b/soh/src/code/speed_meter.c
index b2f491502..8717ae4a5 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/speed_meter.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/speed_meter.c
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@ volatile OSTime gAudioThreadUpdateTimeAcc;
 volatile OSTime gRSPAudioTotalTime;
 volatile OSTime gRSPGFXTotalTime;
 volatile OSTime gRSPOtherTotalTime;
-volatile OSTime D_8016A578;
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was D_8016A578: volatile OSTime sitting inside the RSP/RDP total-time block between gRSPOtherTotalTime and gRDPTotalTime, but never read or written; the slot's original meaning is unknown.
+volatile OSTime gUnusedTotalTime;  // was D_8016A578 [LLM:GUESS]
 volatile OSTime gRDPTotalTime;
 SpeedMeterTimeEntry* sSpeedMeterTimeEntryPtr;
 
